---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.5 · Defender, Piety & Morytania" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-5" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.5</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Defender, Piety & Morytania</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Build lasting melee and Prayer strength while following the Temple Knights and Myreque stories. Alternate quests, Slayer, gear, bones and skill checks; work toward Piety and Sins of the Father in manageable sessions.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Finish the Temple Knight chain, full Legends' Quest, Ghosts Ahoy, Haunted Mine/Tarn, A Kingdom Divided and the Myreque story through Sins; obtain the dragon defender and Piety; finish Troubled Tortugans."
        stats={["60 Attack; Attack + Strength ≥130; 70 Defence and Prayer", "54 Agility, 60 Fletching and 60 Herblore before Sins", "50 Slayer for Sins, then 51 for Troubled Tortugans", "45 Sailing already reached; 45→67 continues in 2.6"]}
        unlocks={["Proselyte, Ectophial, Salve amulet (e), dragon defender and Piety", "Full Legends and 120,000 selectable Herblore XP", "Book of the Dead, Darkmeyer and Hallowed Sepulchre access", "Great Conch and the later Red Reef path"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Before you begin:</strong> have Barrows gloves, 40+ Herblore, 40+ Slayer, 45 Sailing and the Legends' Quest start completed in 2.4. Keep the RFD lamp banked if you are still below 50 Herblore. Check Attack, Strength, Defence, Agility, Prayer and Fletching in your skill tab so you can train only what remains at each step. This is a long chapter; switch between the quests and training sections when you want a break.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Temple Knights · useful XP first</div><h2>Complete the Temple Knight quests and collect their skill rewards.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-black-knights" number="1" title="Complete Black Knights' Fortress">
        <p>Speak to <strong>Sir Amik Varze</strong> in Falador Castle and resolve the Black Knights' weapon plot at the fortress north of Ice Mountain. Bring an <strong>iron chainbody, bronze med helm and cabbage</strong> (not one from Draynor Manor), plus food and a teleport. This short old quest opens Recruitment Drive and is also a hard prerequisite for King's Ransom later. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Black_Knights%27_Fortress" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Buy the two disguise pieces if missing">
          <p>Buy the <strong>bronze med helm from Peksa in Barbarian Village</strong> and the <strong>iron chainbody from Wayne in southern Falador</strong>. Pick a normal cabbage at the farm south of Falador or at Edgeville Monastery; Draynor Manor's cabbage does not work for this sabotage.</p>
          <p>Keep both armour pieces after the quest for King's Ransom. They are separate from the three black-armour pieces needed there.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-recruitment" number="2" title="Complete Recruitment Drive for Herblore, Agility and Prayer XP">
        <p>Visit <strong>Sir Tiffy Cashien in Falador Park</strong> after Black Knights' Fortress. Bank <strong>all equipment and inventory items</strong> for the Temple Knight trials; the rooms contain self-supplied puzzle items. Work through the five randomized tests and the Sir Leye fight as the quest directs. Completion gives <strong>1,000.5 XP each in Herblore, Agility and Prayer</strong>. Claim the rewards before training those skills further; the Herblore XP helps you reach 45 for Legends' Quest. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Recruitment_Drive" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Trial solutions</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-wanted" number="3" title="Complete Wanted! for 5,000 Slayer XP">
        <p>Continue from Sir Tiffy and the Temple Knights to hunt Solus Dellagar. Prepare <strong>20 unnoted rune or pure essence, an enclosed light and a rope if your Lumbridge Swamp entrance is not already roped</strong>. Sir Tiffy makes the <strong>commorb</strong> from one law rune, one enchanted gem and one molten glass, or 10,000 coins; add useful teleports, food and combat gear; follow the commorb's clues from location to location. Its <strong>5,000 Slayer XP</strong> reduces the later Sins gate and it opens The Slug Menace. Check your Slayer level after claiming the reward. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Wanted!" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Prepare the commorb and 20 unnoted essence">
          <p>Buy an <strong>enchanted gem from any Slayer master</strong>, a law rune from the Wizards' Guild, and make <strong>one new molten glass</strong> from charter-shop sand and soda ash at a furnace. The <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a> explains those suppliers and boosted Guild access. Hand all three to Tiffy, or use the 10,000-coin alternative if you prefer.</p>
          <p>If the old essence was crafted, take a pickaxe to <strong>Aubury in Varrock and ask to teleport to the Rune Essence Mine</strong>. Mine until you have 20 rune/pure essence, bank it and withdraw it <strong>unnoted</strong> for the quest. Reuse the enclosed lantern from Tears; Miltog sells a replacement and the still supplies oil from swamp tar. Ned sells a replacement rope.</p>
          <p>Keep the commorb for The Slug Menace; Sir Tiffy replaces it if lost. Buy a spiny helmet from a Slayer master if you want protection when passing the swamp cave's wall beasts.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-temple-eye" number="4" title="Complete Temple of the Eye for Runecraft progress and Guardians access">
        <p><strong>Returning-player primer:</strong> Temple of the Eye starts with <strong>Wizard Persten north of Al Kharid, near the Lumbridge gate and west of the Emir's Arena</strong>, and introduces the Guardians of the Rift (GOTR) portal beneath the Temple. GOTR is a team Runecraft minigame where players gather fragments, craft essence and power a guardian against incoming rifts. Complete the quest tutorial for Runecraft XP and access; further minigame rounds are optional for now. Bring <strong>one bucket of water, a pickaxe and a chisel</strong>, then follow its short tutorial round and dialogues. The quest awards <strong>4,210 Runecraft XP along the way plus 5,000 at completion</strong>, or 9,210 total. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Temple_of_the_Eye" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest and minigame primer</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="The only outside consumable is a bucket of water">
          <p>Buy a bucket from Lumbridge's general store and fill it at a sink or fountain. Bring your own pickaxe/chisel for convenience; the tutorial can provide them if missing. The strong tea, amulet and incantation are obtained from the quest's NPC sequence, so they are not advance shop purchases.</p>
          <p>Keep the pickaxe and chisel afterward. Guardians of the Rift now provides a convenient way into the five altars The Slug Menace needs, without requiring you to own five talismans.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-rc-30" number="5" title="Check for 30 Runecraft before The Slug Menace">
        <p>Chapter 1 left Runecraft around 24. After Lunar Diplomacy and Temple of the Eye's 9,210 XP, check your <strong>unboosted Runecraft level</strong>. If it is still below 30, finish the remaining training with ordinary rune crafting or a few GOTR rounds: gather essence, craft at the opened altars, hand energy to the guardian and bank the runes. Stop at <strong>30</strong>, needed for The Slug Menace.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-slug-menace" number="6" title="Complete The Slug Menace and buy Proselyte">
        <p>With Wanted!, the earlier Sea Slug quest, <strong>30 Runecraft and 30 Slayer</strong> checked, return to Sir Tiffy. Pack the <strong>commorb, one swamp paste, a chisel, at least five rune/pure essence (15–20 gives a practical failure buffer), melee gear, food and travel gear</strong>; the quest follows the slug threat through its investigation. Its final <strong>level-62 enemy must be defeated with Melee</strong>, so do not arrive with only Magic or Ranged equipment. Afterward buy the <strong>Proselyte armour pack from Sir Tiffy</strong> (25,000 coins). Its strong Prayer bonus makes routine Slayer and future prayer-heavy fights less resource-hungry; it is durable account gear, <strong>not</strong> a hard Sins requirement. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Slug_Menace" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest details</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Bring essence and plan the five altar visits">
          <p>Buy <strong>one swamp paste at Port Khazard's general store</strong>. Reclaim a missing commorb from Sir Tiffy. Mine rune/pure essence via Aubury as in Wanted!, then carve the quest's <strong>five blank runes</strong> with the chisel; failed carvings consume essence, so replenish until all five exist. The investigation supplies the dead sea slug and page fragments.</p>
          <p>With Temple of the Eye complete, join a <strong>Guardians of the Rift</strong> round and carry the quest blanks. As the <strong>air, water, earth, fire and mind</strong> Portal Guardians activate, enter the matching altar and use its quest blank on the altar. You meet their level requirements with 30 Runecraft. Wait for a missing portal in a later round if needed; leave once all five blanks are charged.</p>
          <p>Owned talismans/tiaras also work, and the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-4/#i24-lunar`}> Lunar altar-access preparation</a> explains the Abyss alternative and its Wilderness entry. Keep <strong>25,000 coins</strong> separate for Proselyte after the melee-only finale.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <div class="callout"><strong>Ready for a combat break?</strong> Take an ordinary Slayer assignment and train Attack, Strength or Defence. Do as many tasks as you feel like before returning to quests; you need 50 Slayer before Sins and 51 before Troubled Tortugans later on this page.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Zogre and Legends</div><h2>Use quest rewards to reach 45 Herblore.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-zogre" number="7" title="Complete Zogre Flesh Eaters">
        <p>Big Chompy Bird Hunting is already complete. Speak to <strong>Grish in the Jiggig area south of Castle Wars</strong>. Bring a knife, food, a teleport and <strong>Crumble Undead runes</strong> for the straightforward combat option. The alternative is a <strong>comp ogre bow with brutal arrows</strong>, which this quest teaches you to make; the ordinary ogre bow/arrows from Chompy are not that setup. Prepare <strong>Relicym's balm</strong> once the investigation unlocks its recipe. Rebank before <strong>Slash Bash</strong>, use ranged safespots and protection prayers where appropriate, and follow the grave/key clues in the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Zogre_Flesh_Eaters" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a>. Claim <strong>2,000 XP each in Herblore, Fletching and Ranged</strong>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Prepare the disease cure and a weapon that works on zogres">
          <p><strong>Crumble Undead</strong> is a level-39 standard spell using <strong>two air, two earth and one chaos rune per cast</strong>; Aubury sells those runes. Carry a sensible stack and a teleport for a failed attempt. If you choose Ranged, learn the <strong>comp ogre bow and brutal-arrow</strong> recipes from Grish and make that complete setup before Slash Bash, rather than assuming the old chompy kit works.</p>
          <p>After transformed <strong>Sithik Ints</strong> explains the cure, make Relicym's balm at 8 Herblore: <strong>rogue's purse + vial of water + snake weed</strong>. Search the speckled fungus in Karamja's Pothole Dungeon for rogue's purse and the marshy vines southwest of Tai Bwo Wannai for snake weed, the same plants used in Jungle Potion. Show/sell a finished balm to <strong>Uglug Nar outside Jiggig</strong>; his unlocked shop sells more three-dose balms, so buy replacements before the boss. Antipoison does not cure disease.</p>
          <p>The backpack supplies a knife and tankard; Sithik's furniture supplies the portrait paper/charcoal. Extra paper can be taken from his drawers if the portrait fails. The strange potion and gate key are obtained through the investigation.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-herblore-45" number="8" title="Check for 45 Herblore before Legends' Quest">
        <p>Check your Herblore level before making more potions. Starting at level 40's <strong>37,224 XP</strong>, the rewards from Heroes' Quest (<strong>1,325</strong>), both One Small Favour lamps (<strong>20,000</strong>), Recruitment Drive (<strong>1,000.5</strong>) and Zogre (<strong>2,000</strong>) bring you to <strong>61,549.5 XP</strong>. That is just above level 45's <strong>61,512 XP</strong> requirement. If you are below 45, check that you claimed those rewards and used both lamps on Herblore.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-legends" number="9" title="Finish Legends' Quest and put all four rewards into Herblore">
        <p>The 2.4 partial start already supplied the Kharazi map, Radimus notes and vanilla pod. With <strong>45 Herblore</strong>, you can now finish the quest. Check <strong>107+ QP, 50 Agility/Crafting/Strength/Thieving/Woodcutting/Smithing, 56 Magic, 52 Mining and 42 Prayer</strong>, plus the earlier prerequisite quests; the previous steps cover these requirements. Check your journal and skills before returning to the jungle.</p>
        <p><strong>Prepare for the jungle and caves:</strong> keep the <strong>Radimus notes</strong> from 2.4 and stage a <strong>rune-or-better axe, machete, bullroarer, charcoal and 3–5 papyrus</strong> for the jungle. For later phases bank <strong>two gold bars (spares if you can), hammer, rope, two ordinary lockpicks, pickaxe, vial of water, one each cut opal/jade/red topaz/sapphire/emerald/ruby/diamond, mind and soul runes, two law runes, an earth rune, an unpowered orb and runes for a Charge Orb spell</strong> (an extra orb/cast if you take the long cave path). <strong>Charge Orb needs the standard spellbook</strong>, so switch back from Lunar/Ancients before that phase. Ardrigal and snake weed can be obtained during the quest. Withdraw by phase, not in one overloaded inventory.</p>
        <p><strong>Before the demon fights:</strong> Nezikchened is a <strong>level-187 demon fought three times</strong>; he drains Prayer when a fight starts and can use melee and Magic. Bring antipoison for jungle travel, good food, prayer restores, a teleport and a comfortable melee or ranged setup; restore Prayer and use Protect from Melee where the encounter calls for it. The caves have dangerous enemies and several re-entry steps, so bank between sections and read the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Legends%27_Quest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current quest walkthrough</a> for the binding-book and cave sequence. At reward selection choose <strong>Herblore all four times</strong>: 4 × 30,000 = <strong>120,000 Herblore XP</strong>. The same skill may be chosen repeatedly. <strong>Talk to Radimus again after the four choices</strong> to finish the quest and receive its Quest Points.</p>
        <p>If the RFD <strong>20,000-XP lamp</strong> was banked in 2.4, Herblore is now eligible at level 50+, so use it on Herblore. If you already used it on Herblore in 2.4, continue with your current level. Check the skill tab after collecting all of these rewards.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Supply fresh orbs, gems and the jungle return kit">
          <p>If the partial start ended before the bullroarer, use your <strong>completed Radimus notes on a Jungle Forester</strong> to receive one; the same interaction replaces a lost one. Radimus replaces his notes. Jiminua sells machete, charcoal and papyrus. Buy a <strong>rune axe from the Woodcutting Guild shop</strong> if no suitable axe is banked; bring it for the jungle portion.</p>
          <p>Count <strong>one cut opal, jade, red topaz, sapphire, emerald, ruby and diamond</strong>. Mine Shilo's surface gem rocks and cut gems until each missing type is present; replace any low-tier gems that are crushed while cutting. Buy gold ore from Ordan and smelt at least <strong>two gold bars</strong>, with more if the gold-bowl attempt needs a retry. Buy ordinary lockpicks from <strong>Martin Thwait in the Rogues' Den</strong>, whose 50 Agility/Thieving access is already met; Ned supplies rope.</p>
          <p>Make <strong>two new unpowered orbs</strong> from two molten glass with a glassblowing pipe (46 Crafting): the 1,590 old orbs were charged and alched. For the supported <strong>Charge Earth Orb</strong> choice, take <strong>six cosmic and 60 earth runes</strong> for two possible gate casts, plus the separate wall offerings of <strong>one mind, one soul, two law and one earth rune</strong>. Baba Yaga sells cosmic/elemental runes after Lunar; the Wizards' Guild sells law/soul runes. Use the standard spellbook.</p>
          <p>Buy a vial of water from Jatix in Taverley. Obtain ardrigal from the palms on northeast Karamja and snake weed from the marshy vines southwest of Tai Bwo Wannai during the quest. Refill the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> and food before each demon section.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Morytania utility</div><h2>Open travel and an undead-specific tool, then break into combat.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-ghosts" number="10" title="Complete Ghosts Ahoy; keep the Ectophial">
        <p>Bring the <strong>ghostspeak amulet</strong>, Chapter 1's <strong>10 banked buckets of slime</strong>, bones and empty pots for bonemeal, <strong>nettle tea in a bowl</strong>, a bucket of milk, silk, dyes, spade, oak longbow, knife, needle/thread and roughly 400 coins. Animal Magnetism used the 20 ecto-tokens collected in Chapter 1. Check any newly earned tokens first. The usual quest route needs <strong>31 tokens without an activated ring of charos</strong> (20 with one; 25/10 if using the charter shortcut). At the Ectofuntus, grind a bone upstairs into a pot of bonemeal, pair it with one banked bucket of slime, worship, then talk to a ghost disciple while wearing the amulet for <strong>five tokens per offering</strong>. Seven offerings yield 35 tokens from zero, so the 10 saved slime buckets suffice; make only the shortfall. At Port Phasmatys, help Velorina, acquire the ghost disguise and petition signatures, and resolve Necrovarus's hold on the ghosts; the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ghosts_Ahoy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a> handles the variable dyes and map clues. Claim <strong>2,400 Prayer XP</strong> before estimating your 70-Prayer bone budget.</p>
        <p>The <strong>Ectophial</strong> teleports to the Ectofuntus/Port Phasmatys region and refills at the Ectofuntus. Keep it permanently: it shortens this chapter's eastern Morytania trips. The port is also permanently accessible without paying tokens.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Make the tea and replace each consumed token/disguise supply">
          <p>Pick <strong>nettles while wearing gloves</strong>, for example near Edgeville's yews. Add them to a bowl of water and heat the bowl on a range. Bring that <strong>nettle tea</strong> and a separate bucket of milk; the Old Crone provides the porcelain cup, then asks for milk after the tea is in her cup. An ordinary cup of tea or Guthix rest is not this recipe.</p>
          <p>Count your slime now: a zero-token plan using seven offerings needs <strong>seven buckets for 35 tokens plus one separate bucket for the ghost disguise</strong>. If the earlier ten are gone, take empty buckets down to the Ectofuntus slime pool and refill them. Kill chickens for ordinary bones and buy pots for the bonemeal; each additional offering replaces five spent tokens. Reclaim a lost ghostspeak amulet from Father Urhney in Lumbridge Swamp.</p>
          <p>Inspect the ship's flag colours before buying only the needed dyes. Aggie in Draynor makes <strong>red from three redberries, yellow from two onions, or blue from two woad leaves</strong>, plus five coins each; Wyson in Falador Park sells two woad leaves for 20 coins. Mix primary dyes if a flag needs a secondary colour. Three of each primary covers any three-colour combination if you prefer a buffer. Buy silk in Al Kharid, needle/thread at Dommik and a <strong>strung oak longbow</strong> from Lowe in Varrock.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Fletching break</div><h2>Switch out of quest mode before the next Morytania stretch.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-fletching-60" number="11" title="Reach 60 Fletching for Sins">
        <p>Check your Fletching level after Chapter 1 and Zogre's 2,000 XP; Sins requires <strong>unboosted 60</strong>. If still below 50, bridge the high-40s with <strong>willow longbows</strong> or the existing arrow-making supplies. At <strong>50</strong>, switch to banked-maple <strong>shortbows</strong>; at <strong>55</strong>, maple <strong>longbows</strong> become available. Use a knife and ordinary <strong>Make-X</strong>. If your kingdom's teak stock for Construction is healthy, temporarily move its five non-herb workers from teaks to <strong>maples</strong> for passive logs/nests; collect them when convenient. If no maple stock has accumulated, <strong>cut maples north of Seers' Village bank</strong> with your axe; 45 Woodcutting is already covered. Below 50 Fletching, cut willows at Draynor for the willow-longbow bridge. Use your current XP to judge how many bows to make; cut logs yourself if you want to continue before the next kingdom collection. Stop when the skill tab reads 60. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fletching_training" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Fletching methods</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i25-fletch-methods" informational={true} skill="Fletching" target="60, unboosted" why="Sins has an unboostable Fletching gate; extra levels do not unlock this chapter." recommended="Willow longbows or existing arrows below 50; banked/kingdom maple shortbows from 50, longbows from 55, using Make-X." resource="Vale Totems if you want an active, higher-XP-per-log change of pace." fast="Broad arrows from 52 only if you independently choose the 300-Slayer-point Broader Fletching unlock and its expense." />
      </RouteStep>

      <ExpandableNote label="Optional Fletching method" title="Vale Totems: a modern active change of pace">
        <p>If you prefer moving around to bankstanding, visit <strong>Ranulph in north-west Auburn Valley, Varlamore</strong> (fairy ring <strong>AIS</strong> is one route). The short <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Vale_Totems_(miniquest)" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Vale Totems miniquest</a> requires Children of the Sun and 20 Fletching and teaches the activity. For the miniquest itself, cut <strong>five oak logs</strong> and use a knife to fletch four into <strong>oak shortbows (u)</strong>; keep the fifth as a log. That supplies the <strong>one oak log and four matching oak items</strong> needed to build and decorate the taught totem. A knife spawns in Lumbridge Castle's kitchen if missing. After the miniquest, repeat with one log and four matching-wood fletched items per totem. Ent visits generate <strong>offerings and research points</strong> for rewards; totems eventually need rebuilding. Maple totems open at 50 Fletching. It is more active than making bows at a bank; try it if that sounds more enjoyable. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Vale_Totems" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full totem primer</a>.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <section><div class="section-label">Morytania utility, continued</div><h2>Now explore the mine and Tarn's lair.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-haunted" number="12" title="Complete Haunted Mine and make a Salve amulet">
        <p>Go to the <strong>Abandoned Mine west of Mort'ton</strong> (the Morytania route is easier with the Ectophial/fairy rings). Bring <strong>chisel, ball of wool, light source, food, prayer restore and Magic/Ranged combat gear</strong>; the mine's carts, levers and glowing fungus form a connected puzzle, so use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Haunted_Mine" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current map/lever walkthrough</a>. Bank before <strong>Treus Dayth</strong>: he moves/invises and the machinery hits hard. Protect from Missiles and a ranged or Crumble Undead setup are practical; restock if food runs low; dying here loses items under the usual death rules. After winning, cut a <strong>salve shard</strong> from the crystal outcrop and string it with wool.</p>
        <p>Keep the Salve amulet for <strong>undead</strong> opponents only. It is not a universal Morytania-vampyre or Sins-boss damage bonus, and its melee effect does not stack with a black mask/Slayer helm.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover the amulet materials and use the mine's own light puzzle">
          <p>Buy a chisel from a general store and spin one ball of wool at Lumbridge if the previous quests used yours. The <strong>glowing fungus inside the mine</strong> supplies the light for its deeper section: follow the mine-cart transport puzzle, because an ordinary lamp does not replace it there.</p>
          <p>Take food, a working teleport and the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> for Treus Dayth. After the fight, the crystal outcrop supplies replacement salve shards if you later need another amulet; each replacement still needs its own wool.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-tarn" number="13" title="Complete Lair of Tarn Razorlor and enchant the Salve amulet">
        <p>Haunted Mine opens <strong>Tarn's Lair</strong> and 2.3 already gave unboosted <strong>40+ Slayer</strong>. Enter the maze with a <strong>light source, food, antipoison, prayer restore and a teleport</strong>; keep enough supplies for level-100 Tarn and the dungeon monsters, and consult the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Lair_of_Tarn_Razorlor" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">maze route</a> rather than wandering blind. Claim <strong>5,000 Slayer XP</strong> and use <strong>Tarn's diary on the Salve amulet</strong> for Salve (e). Check your Slayer level afterward and keep the amulet for undead enemies.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Check the amulet and combat supplies before entering the maze">
          <p>The miniquest has no outside puzzle-material shopping list. Carry your <strong>Salve amulet</strong> for the diary upgrade, or cut another shard in the completed Haunted Mine and string it with fresh wool. Tarn's diary is collected in the room beyond the fight. Refill food, antipoison and prayer doses through the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> before committing to the maze.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <div class="callout"><strong>Take a break to gather bones:</strong> after Recruitment Drive and Ghosts Ahoy, check your Prayer XP and banked dragon bones. If you want a change from quests, gather one or two inventories using the Isle of Souls method below, then return to the story. You can spread the training to 70 Prayer across several sessions.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Myreque, first leg</div><h2>Establish Burgh de Rott; let quests interrupt melee training.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-in-search" number="14" title="Complete In Search of the Myreque">
        <p>From <strong>Canifis</strong>, speak to Vanstrom Klause and carry weapons to the Myreque hidden south in Mort Myre. Bank <strong>one steel longsword, two steel swords, a steel mace, warhammer and dagger</strong>; bring <strong>six ordinary planks, hammer, 225 steel nails, a charged druid pouch, a silver weapon, food and 10 coins</strong>. If the exact steel weapons are missing, smith them from nine steel bars at a normal anvil; your 50 Smithing clears every recipe. Cross the swamp with pouch charges, repair Cyreg's boat, then fight the <strong>Skeleton Hellhound</strong> at the hideout. This is the first of five connected story quests; finish it before changing regions. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/In_Search_of_the_Myreque" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest route</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Make the exact delivery and refill the druid pouch">
          <p>The weapon set costs <strong>nine steel bars</strong>: longsword two, two swords one each, mace one, warhammer three and dagger one. Buy iron/coal from Ordan and smelt the deficit. The <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a> supplies <strong>six regular planks and 225 steel nails</strong>; these are separate from the planks and nails consumed by earlier bridges and Cold War.</p>
          <p>Charge the druid pouch to <strong>at least five</strong>, with extra for ghasts on the journey: use <strong>Bloom on a blessed silver sickle near Mort Myre's rotten logs, twigs and bushes</strong>, collect the resulting plants and fill the pouch. Restore Prayer and repeat until the charge count is sufficient. If the pouch or blessed sickle is gone, return to the Nature Spirit's grotto; make a replacement silver sickle from one silver bar and a sickle mould if needed, then have it blessed.</p>
          <p>Keep the delivery weapons distinct from your own combat weapon. Bring the charged pouch, silver weapon, food, ten coins and a teleport for the swamp trip.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-in-aid" number="15" title="Complete In Aid of the Myreque; use the 15 banked salmon">
        <p>Return to <strong>Veliaf behind the Canifis pub</strong> and help establish Burgh de Rott. Stage <strong>11 ordinary planks, 44 nails, hammer, pickaxe, spade, five buckets, two swamp paste, two steel bars, one coal and four tinderboxes</strong> for the town repairs (some nails can be found during the quest). The general store asks for <strong>10 bronze axes, three tinderboxes and 10 raw mackerel or snail meats</strong>; check its request before collecting the fish/meat. For the Ivandis rod, later stage <strong>one soft clay, one silver bar, one mithril bar, one cut sapphire, one rope, one cosmic and one water rune for Lvl-1 Enchant</strong>; switch to the <strong>standard spellbook</strong> for that cast if needed. Use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/In_Aid_of_the_Myreque" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a> for the repair order and coffin/rod details.</p>
        <p><strong>Food for Ivan's escort:</strong> withdraw the <strong>15 reserved salmon</strong>, cook them if they are still raw, then give the <strong>cooked salmon</strong> to Ivan Strom for his escort, together with a steel med helm, chainbody, platelegs and silver sickle if banked. Pack your own food separately from Ivan's salmon. Complete the escort and keep the <strong>rod of Ivandis</strong> for the later chain. This quest also grants <strong>2,000 XP each in Attack, Strength, Crafting and Defence</strong>; check your new combat levels before training.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Refill town repairs, requested stock and Ivan's separate food">
          <p>Bring <strong>one spare food item for the entry chest</strong>, then stage the repairs at the bank. Buy <strong>11 regular planks and 44 nails</strong> via the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a>; buy buckets/tinderboxes from a general store and <strong>two swamp paste at Port Khazard</strong>. Four tinderboxes means three for the shop hand-in plus one to light the furnace. Keep <strong>two steel bars and one coal</strong> separate for that furnace.</p>
          <p>Buy <strong>ten bronze axes from Bob in Lumbridge</strong>, waiting for stock or changing worlds if needed. After learning the food request, big-net fish at Catherby until you have <strong>ten raw mackerel</strong>, or kill Mort Myre snails for <strong>ten raw snail meats</strong> if that is the requested option. Cooked fish cannot satisfy this hand-in. Carry a silver weapon for the Gadderanks/vampyre section. If your silver sickle is missing, use <strong>one additional silver bar and Dommik's sickle mould at a furnace (18 Crafting)</strong> to make another; this bar is separate from the rod's bar.</p>
          <p>For the rod, mine one silver ore at Al Kharid and smelt a bar; buy one mithril ore and four coal from Ordan and smelt the mithril bar. Make fresh soft clay, mine/cut a sapphire at Shilo if missing, buy rope from Ned and the two enchant runes from Baba Yaga. Follow the quest's mould and coffin instructions with these materials.</p>
          <p>If the <strong>15 salmon</strong> were eaten or otherwise spent, fly-fish at Lumbridge's river or Shilo with a fly-fishing rod and feathers from Gerrant; keep and cook salmon until 15 cooked ones are banked. They are Ivan's escort food, in addition to your own. His optional steel med helm/chainbody/platelegs and silver sickle can be smithed if you want the extra protection, and you can complete the escort without it.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <div class="callout"><strong>Fit Slayer between quests:</strong> take tasks from a master appropriate to your combat level, ask about required special gear, and use Proselyte when Prayer bonus helps. Work on Attack, Strength or Defence according to the next requirement. Stop to quest, fletch or gather bones whenever that feels better. Ordinary assignments and combat equipment are enough.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Melee upgrade</div><h2>Check your levels and work toward the next weapon upgrade.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-attack-60" number="16" title="Reach 60 Attack and use the dragon scimitar">
        <p>After In Aid's combat XP and any Slayer work, check the skill tab. Train only the shortfall to <strong>unboosted 60 Attack</strong>. This makes the <strong>dragon scimitar unlocked by Monkey Madness I in 2.2</strong> usable as a normal melee weapon. Use ordinary Slayer assignments first; if a short gap remains when you want the weapon, the relaxed <strong>Gemstone Crab</strong> or another low-attention target is fine. If you trained Attack earlier, skip any target you already meet.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-combined-130" number="17" title="Reach Attack + Strength ≥130 for the Warriors' Guild">
        <p>Add your <strong>unboosted Attack and Strength levels</strong>. After Attack 60, train Strength only until the sum reaches <strong>at least 130</strong>; this often resembles 60/70, but extra quest or Slayer XP may make an exact 70 Strength unnecessary. Prefer task combat; if Slayer gets to 50 first, finish only this remaining sum at Gemstone Crab or another relaxed training spot. Players who did optional 65/65/65 can skip any targets already met.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i25-melee-methods" informational={true} skill="Melee" target="60 Attack, then 130 combined" why="60 Attack lets you wield the dragon scimitar; 130 combined Attack and Strength opens the Warriors' Guild." recommended="Ordinary Slayer tasks, changing attack styles as you reach each target." relaxed="Gemstone Crab for only a remaining combat gap after quest and Slayer XP." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-defence-60" number="18" title="Reach 60 Defence to equip the dragon defender">
        <p>Read Defence after In Aid and ordinary combat. Train only the remainder to <strong>unboosted 60</strong>, preferably while progressing Slayer; use a low-attention combat spot if task RNG leaves a gap. The guild can be entered by the Attack + Strength sum, but the <strong>dragon defender itself cannot be equipped below 60 Defence</strong>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-defender" number="19" title="Earn and keep the dragon defender">
        <p>Enter the <strong>Warriors' Guild west of Burthorpe</strong> once Attack + Strength is at least 130. For tokens, the simple starting activity is <strong>animated armour</strong>: bring a spare full metal set (helm, platebody, legs), animate it in the guild's animation room, defeat it and recover the pieces. Bank/refill tokens in modest trips; no giant stockpile is required. Bring food and the best available melee kit. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Warriors%27_Guild" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guild and token guide</a>.</p>
        <p>Spend tokens to fight <strong>upstairs Cyclopes</strong>. Their defenders advance in order: <strong>bronze → iron → steel → black → mithril → adamant → rune</strong>. Show the <strong>rune defender</strong> to the guild attendant for <strong>basement Cyclopes</strong>, then keep fighting until the <strong>dragon defender</strong> drops. Keep the defender and a backup rune defender if convenient; equip dragon at unboosted 60 Defence. Stop when you have the dragon defender; the number of kills and tokens needed will vary. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dragon_defender" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Defender progression</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Make an animation set if no complete spare set is banked">
          <p>A <strong>steel full helm, steel platebody and steel platelegs</strong> use <strong>ten steel bars</strong> at an anvil: two, five and three respectively. 50 Smithing already clears the highest recipe, so smelt only missing bars from Ordan's iron/coal. A med helm or chainbody does not complete this set.</p>
          <p>Recover the armour after each animated kill. If a piece is destroyed, remake that piece before the next animation. The guild food shop can replace food while you work on tokens and defenders; restock between trips until the dragon defender drops.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Myreque and Kourend</div><h2>Trade the guild grind for a story quest, an Agility stop and a different region.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-darkness" number="20" title="Complete Darkness of Hallowvale; allocate all three choices to Herblore">
        <p>Start from <strong>Veliaf in Burgh de Rott</strong> after In Aid. Meiyerditch is a <strong>maze-like occupied city</strong>: prepare weight-reducing clothing, food, restores, <strong>knife, hammer, two regular planks and eight nails</strong>, plus the rod of Ivandis and travel supplies. Use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Darkness_of_Hallowvale" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current city traversal map</a> for roofs, barricades and the castle sketches rather than trying to memorize every turn. Bank before dangerous sections; do the city reconnaissance as one coherent quest.</p>
        <p>Claim <strong>7,000 Agility, 6,000 Thieving and 2,000 Construction XP</strong>. Its three selectable <strong>2,000-XP rewards</strong> all go into <strong>Herblore</strong> (6,000 total). Check your <strong>Agility and Herblore levels</strong> afterward; A Kingdom Divided needs 54 Agility and 50 Herblore.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Prepare the boat materials and collect the sketch supplies">
          <p>Buy or make the <strong>two regular planks and eight nails</strong> using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/#i22-dragon-slayer`}> small-material suppliers</a>. Keep your hammer and knife through the city section. A miner can provide a pickaxe if you are sent to the mines, and the quest supplies the charcoal and papyrus for its castle sketches; you do not need another bulk jungle-mapping purchase.</p>
          <p>Bank and refill food and ordinary restores through the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> before the dangerous scouting. Keep the rod of Ivandis from In Aid for the continuing chain.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-agility-54" number="21" title="Reach 54 Agility for A Kingdom Divided">
        <p>Check your Agility level after Darkness of Hallowvale. If it is below 54, train only as much as you still need. The recommended lower-input course is the <strong>basic Colossal Wyrm Agility Course</strong> (opens at 50) at the <strong>Colossal Wyrm Remains in the Avium Savannah, Varlamore</strong>. Travel via Varlamore's roads or an available transport, speak to <strong>Worm Tongue</strong> at the course, then follow the scaffolding obstacles for a complete lap. Termites are scooped automatically at some obstacles and can buy small rewards; any blessed bone shards you buy give extra Prayer XP. The longer obstacle animations make this a lower-input option. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Colossal_agility" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Course and access map</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Falador rooftop</strong> is the level-50 alternative: start at its southern wall, finish the rooftop loop and collect marks of grace as available. Neither Hallowed Sepulchre nor Brimhaven is required. Stop at <strong>unboosted 54</strong>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i25-agility-methods" informational={true} skill="Agility" target="54, unboosted" why="A Kingdom Divided's gate is unboostable." recommended="Basic Colossal Wyrm course: longer animations and fewer inputs per lap." relaxed="Falador rooftop from 50 if you prefer a familiar loop and marks of grace." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-kingdom" number="22" title="Complete A Kingdom Divided; use both lamps on Herblore">
        <p>Check <strong>unboosted 54 Agility, 52 Thieving, 52 Woodcutting, 50 Herblore, 42 Mining, 38 Crafting and 35 Magic</strong>; these are unboostable, and full Legends' XP covers Herblore 50. The earlier route completed <strong>The Depths of Despair, The Queen of Thieves, The Ascent of Arceuus, The Forsaken Tower and Tale of the Righteous</strong>. <strong>Architectural Alliance is removed and is not a prerequisite.</strong></p>
        <p>Start with <strong>Martin Holt at Kourend Castle</strong>. Stage an axe, <strong>defence potion(3) or (4), volcanic sulphur, molten glass, dark essence block or pickaxe/chisel</strong>, fire-combat runes and food; the quest requires a <strong>standard-spellbook Fire Bolt or a stronger fire spell</strong>, so switch from Lunar/Ancients if necessary. It has several separated fights, including a melee-only target and Xamphur; bank between sections and use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Kingdom_Divided" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a> for the Kourend travel order. Claim the <strong>Book of the Dead</strong> and use <strong>both 10,000-XP lamps on Herblore</strong>. Check your new Herblore level.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Buy the exact defence potion and prepare both untradeable materials">
          <p>With the Warriors' Guild now open, buy <strong>one defence potion(3) from Lilly</strong> inside the guild. Keep all three doses for the quest's mixture; a one- or two-dose leftover is insufficient. Buying it saves a ranarr and whiteberries for other potions.</p>
          <p>Mine <strong>one volcanic sulphur in Lovakengj</strong> with a pickaxe; a face mask from a Slayer master helps with the clouds. Mine <strong>one dense essence block in Arceuus</strong> with a pickaxe and chisel, then use it on the <strong>Dark Altar</strong> to make the dark essence block. You already meet the Mining and Crafting requirements. Make one new molten glass from charter sand/soda ash if the bank has none.</p>
          <p>Pack runes for <strong>Fire Bolt or better</strong>; the simplest Fire Bolt cast needs three air, four fire and one chaos rune, all sold by Aubury. Bring the melee gear required by the melee-only fight and bank between encounters. Refill the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> and food for the final section.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <div class="callout"><strong>Ready for another change of pace?</strong> After Kourend, take a Slayer task or gather another inventory of blue-dragon bones. Work toward 50 Slayer and 70 Prayer, checking your progress between trips.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Defence, Camelot and Myreque</div><h2>Claim the big Defence rewards before paying for the last levels.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-defence-65" number="23" title="Reach 65 Defence for King's Ransom">
        <p>Use your dragon scimitar/defender on ordinary Slayer assignments where reasonable, training Defence only until the skill tab reads <strong>unboosted 65</strong>. If Slayer reaches its next gate first, use Gemstone Crab or another relaxed target for only the remaining Defence XP. Do <strong>not</strong> train 65→70 yet: King's Ransom and Knight Waves award Defence XP that would otherwise be overshot.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-kings-ransom" number="24" title="Complete King's Ransom; send the lamp to Herblore">
        <p>Check <strong>unboosted 65 Defence and 45 Magic</strong>. You have already completed <strong>Black Knights' Fortress</strong> above, <strong>Holy Grail/Merlin's Crystal</strong> from 1.3, and <strong>Murder Mystery/One Small Favour</strong> from 2.4. Begin with the <strong>Gossip outside Sinclair Mansion</strong>. Stage <strong>granite, an <strong>Animate rock scroll</strong>, a lockpick or Telekinetic Grab runes, <strong>black full helm, black platebody, black platelegs</strong>, bronze med helm and iron chainbody</strong>; the last two may still be banked from Black Knights' Fortress. Follow the mansion evidence/court case, visit Wizard Cromperty and release King Arthur as the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/King%27s_Ransom" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a> directs. Claim <strong>33,000 Defence and 5,000 Magic XP</strong>, then use its <strong>5,000-XP level-50+ lamp on Herblore</strong>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace the disguises, granite and Animate rock scroll">
          <p>Reclaim the <strong>Animate rock scroll from Wizard Cromperty in East Ardougne</strong> during the quest if you kept no copy after One Small Favour. Mine <strong>one granite of any size</strong> at the quarry south of the Bandit Camp with your pickaxe; bring desert water for the trip. This is granite, not a granite weapon or limestone.</p>
          <p>The <strong>black full helm and platelegs</strong> are sold by Valaine in the Champions' Guild, and <strong>black platebody</strong> by Horvik in Varrock. Phoenix Gang players may not have bought them for Heroes; Black Arm players must still replace any lost pieces. Recover the bronze med helm from Peksa and iron chainbody from Wayne if Black Knights' Fortress gear was discarded.</p>
          <p>Take an ordinary lockpick from Martin Thwait, or <strong>one law and one air rune</strong> for Telekinetic Grab on the standard spellbook. The knights can also help provide a lockpick inside. Prepare these before continuing into the fortress.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-knight-waves" number="25" title="Complete Knight Waves and claim all four combat rewards">
        <p>Return to <strong>Camelot's training grounds</strong> after King's Ransom. Bring melee gear, <strong>dragon defender, Barrows gloves, strong food and stat restore potions</strong>. Inside Knight Waves, <strong>only Melee works: Prayer, Magic and Ranged cannot be used</strong>, and the knights drain your combat stats. On ordinary accounts this is a safe activity, so you can regear and retry if an attempt fails. Read the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Knight_Waves_Training_Grounds" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">wave mechanics</a> before entering. Completion awards <strong>20,000 XP each in Attack, Strength, Defence and Hitpoints</strong> and opens Chivalry/Piety once their level gates are met. <strong>Read Defence again</strong> before any final 70 grind.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Rebuild ordinary restores and food after the quest fights">
          <p>Check the <strong>ordinary restore-potion doses</strong> remaining after the Culinaromancer and Morytania fights. At 22 Herblore, a harralander + vial of water + red spiders' eggs makes restore(3); use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> to replace missing ingredients. Prayer potions do not restore drained Attack/Strength/Defence here.</p>
          <p>Lilly's Warriors' Guild shop sells three-dose attack, strength and defence potions if you want cheap combat boosts; take separate restore potions for repeated drains. Refill strong food with the 2.4 karambwan loop or the guild food shop, and retry in manageable attempts.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-taste" number="26" title="Complete A Taste of Hope; keep the medallion and flail">
        <p>Return to the Myreque chain from Darkness with <strong>unboosted 48 Crafting, 45 Agility, 40 Attack, 40 Herblore and 38 Slayer</strong> already cleared. Stage the <strong>rod of Ivandis, one cut emerald, a chisel, <strong>one vial of water, 1,000 coins, one cosmic and three air runes</strong> (or an enchant-emerald tablet), food, prayer restore and combat gear</strong>. The quest moves between Meiyerditch and Ver Sinhaza, improves the Ivandis weapon and ends with <strong>Ranis Drakan</strong>; rebank before the abomination and final melee fight. Use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Taste_of_Hope" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current boss/quest guide</a> for exact cues.</p>
        <p>Put all <strong>three 2,500-XP choices into Herblore</strong> (7,500 total). Keep the <strong>Ivandis flail</strong> for the Sins weapon upgrade and <strong>Drakan's medallion</strong>: its free Ver Sinhaza teleport greatly shortens repeated Morytania travel. This is the fourth Myreque quest; Fletching 60 is already checked, but do not enter the fifth until the remaining Slayer, Prayer, Defence and Herblore preparation below.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover the rod and bring the exact emerald-enchantment materials">
          <p>If the rod of Ivandis was lost, speak to Vertida in the new Myreque base during the quest, then get a replacement from <strong>Veliaf in Burgh de Rott</strong>. Mine and cut gems at Shilo until you have one emerald if the bank lacks it. Buy the cosmic/air runes from <strong>Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle</strong> and use <strong>Lvl-2 Enchant on the standard spellbook</strong>.</p>
          <p>The base's northwest crate provides a <strong>blessed silver sickle</strong> for the upgrade. The laboratory supplies its mysterious herb, vial and pestle and mortar, and the broken fountain can fill the vial. Bring the separate vial of water and 1,000 coins listed above for the quest's other requests. Refill the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> before Ranis.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Prepare for Sins of the Father</div><h2>Several different small stops, each with a reason.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-prayer-70" number="27" title="Check your Prayer XP and gather bones in batches to reach 70">
        <p><strong>Why:</strong> Piety needs unboosted 70 Prayer. The number of bones you need depends on your remaining XP. First claim Recruitment Drive and Ghosts Ahoy Prayer XP, read your <strong>current Prayer XP</strong>, and subtract it from the level-70 threshold. Dragon bones give <strong>72 base XP</strong>. The Wilderness <strong>Chaos Altar</strong> gives <strong>350%</strong> per offering and a <strong>50% chance not to consume</strong> that bone; each starting bone therefore yields <strong>504 expected XP</strong> over repeated offerings. Plan <strong>ceil(XP still needed ÷ 504)</strong>, subtract dragon bones already banked, then add a sensible buffer for altar RNG, deaths and mistakes. <strong>504 is an expectation, not a guarantee.</strong> Check your XP after each batch and stop at unboosted 70. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Pay-to-play_Prayer_training" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Chaos Altar mechanics</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Safe/default bone supplier:</strong> <strong>Isle of Souls blue dragons</strong>. Use fairy ring <strong>BJP</strong> on the north coast, run south-east to the dungeon, and find the blue-dragon room's <strong>cove by the adamantite rocks</strong> (check the map before engaging). Attack from behind the terrain with <strong>Water spells or Ranged</strong>; bring an anti-dragon shield/dragonfire protection for travel and any approach mistakes, food, runes/ammo and a teleport. Prioritize <strong>dragon bones</strong>; take hides too if you want them for extra Crafting or cash. Bank at the <strong>Soul Wars lobby</strong> via its minigame teleport or another convenient bank, then return via BJP. The <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Isle_of_Souls_Dungeon" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">dungeon guide</a> marks the safespot. Split collection across sessions around quests and Slayer.</p>
        <p><strong>At the altar:</strong> the Wilderness risk is real even if the bones came from safe dragons. Use disposable gear and small, <strong>unnoted one-inventory trips</strong>; bank your valuable kit and expect possible PK losses. If you decline Wilderness entirely, use a safer Prayer method but recalculate the bone quantity because the 504-XP expectation no longer applies. <strong>Wilderness green dragons</strong> are a faster optional bone source only if you voluntarily accept PK risk; you can finish the chapter using the Isle of Souls instead.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i25-prayer-methods" informational={true} skill="Prayer" target="70, unboosted" why="Piety needs 70 Prayer; use your current XP and altar results to decide how many more bones to gather." recommended="Isle of Souls blue dragons for bones; small disposable Chaos Altar inventories if accepting altar risk." relaxed="Keep blue-dragon collection and altar offerings in separate short sessions; check your remaining XP between them." fast="Wilderness green dragons only by informed opt-in; their faster bones come with PK exposure." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-slayer-50" number="28" title="Reach 50 Slayer before Sins">
        <p>Check the skill tab after <strong>Royal Trouble's 5,000 XP</strong> in 2.3, Wanted!'s <strong>5,000</strong>, Tarn's <strong>5,000</strong> and every ordinary task you chose between this chapter's blocks. Train <strong>only the remaining XP to unboosted 50</strong> with regular assignments; use your normal combat setup and take breaks between tasks. Do <strong>not</strong> insist on 51 yet—that level belongs after Sins and before Troubled Tortugans.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-piety" number="29" title="Finish 70 Defence and unlock Piety">
        <p>Knight Waves is complete and its <strong>20,000 Defence XP</strong> has already been claimed, as has King's Ransom's <strong>33,000</strong>. Check your Defence level now; train <strong>only the remaining gap to unboosted 70</strong> through Slayer or a relaxed combat spot. With <strong>unboosted 70 Prayer</strong> from the preceding bone block and Knight Waves complete, <strong>Piety is unlocked</strong>. This is the chapter's major combat milestone: Barrows gloves, Helm of Neitiznot, dragon scimitar (or best available weapon), dragon defender, Proselyte where Prayer bonus matters, and Piety give you a solid combat kit. A fighter torso or berserker ring is optional.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-herblore-60" number="30" title="Reach 60 Herblore before Sins, then stop">
        <p><strong>Why grind now?</strong> Sins rewards a tome with <strong>six 15,000-XP choices</strong> in a skill at level 60 or above, and all six can go to the same skill. Reaching unboosted 60 <em>before claiming it</em> lets Herblore receive <strong>90,000 XP</strong>. Starting at level 40, your XP after these quest rewards is <strong>37,224</strong> + <strong>1,325</strong> Heroes + <strong>20,000</strong> One Small Favour + <strong>1,000.5</strong> Recruitment + <strong>2,000</strong> Zogre + <strong>120,000</strong> Legends + <strong>20,000</strong> RFD + <strong>5,000</strong> King's + <strong>20,000</strong> A Kingdom Divided + <strong>6,000</strong> Darkness + <strong>7,500</strong> A Taste = <strong>240,049.5 XP</strong>. Level 60 begins at <strong>273,742 XP</strong>, so you need at most <strong>33,692.5 more Herblore XP</strong>—roughly 34k—if you have claimed these rewards. Any potions you have made reduce that further. If you used the RFD lamp on another skill, you will need up to 20k more Herblore XP; check your skill tab for the amount remaining.</p>
        <p>Check your <strong>current Herblore XP</strong> and make only the remaining XP in potions your account will use, from <strong>banked herbs/secondaries, kingdom herbs and Farming Contract or herb-run supplies</strong>. Prioritize useful combat/prayer/antipoison potions rather than stockpiling an arbitrary herb count. Stop at <strong>unboosted 60</strong>; the later level-70 SotE requirement is not this chapter's grind. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Herblore_training" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Herblore method reference</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i25-herblore-methods" informational={true} skill="Herblore" target="60, unboosted, before Sins" why="This precise stop turns Sins' six rewards into 90,000 Herblore XP." recommended="Use banked and kingdom herbs for potions you will actually drink; check your XP between batches." resource="Use herb runs and Farming Contracts for more supplies while training toward 60." />
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Story finale and a return to Sailing</div><h2>Claim the Sins payoff, then open the Great Conch.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i25-sins" number="31" title="Complete Sins of the Father; put all six tome choices into Herblore">
        <p><strong>Required unboosted levels:</strong> <strong>62 Woodcutting, 60 Fletching, 56 Crafting, 52 Agility, 50 Attack, 50 Slayer and 49 Magic</strong>. The earlier quests and training cover these levels; check each in the skill tab. Also confirm <strong>unboosted 60 Herblore before claiming the tome</strong>, unboosted 70 Prayer/Defence, Piety and a working dragon defender. You can use the combat gear obtained so far; a fighter torso and berserker ring are optional.</p>
        <p><strong>Item bank check:</strong> Ivandis flail, <strong>one cut ruby, one cosmic and five fire runes</strong> for Lvl-3 Enchant, axe, knife, chisel, and a <strong>Vyrewatch top, legs and shoes or 1,950 coins</strong>. Begin with <strong>Veliaf outside Slepe church</strong>. Follow the quest's Darkmeyer/Meiyerditch story, turn the <strong>Ivandis flail into the Blisterwood flail</strong> as instructed, and bank/regear before <strong>Vanstrom Klause</strong>. Bring the flail, Barrows gloves, defender, Helm of Neitiznot or suitable headgear, high-healing food, prayer restores and sensible combat potions. During the first phase use <strong>Protect from Magic and Piety</strong>, kill the summoned bloodveld promptly, avoid/lure around the blood orb, and turn away for his darkness cue. In the second phase protection prayers no longer solve the damage: move off marked lightning tiles and keep healing. Study the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Sins_of_the_Father" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current boss cues</a> before a serious attempt; restock and try again if an attempt fails.</p>
        <p>Completion opens <strong>Darkmeyer and Hallowed Sepulchre</strong> as an option. Keep the <strong>Blisterwood flail and Drakan's medallion</strong>. Use the tome <strong>all six times on Herblore</strong> for <strong>90,000 XP</strong>, then check your new Herblore level.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Prepare the disguise and Blisterwood-flail ingredients">
          <p>Buy missing <strong>Vyrewatch top, legs and shoes from Trader Sven</strong> in southern Meiyerditch near Old Man Ral's house, for 1,950 coins for the complete set. This is the earlier shop disguise; the quest later provides its separate noble disguise. If the <strong>Ivandis flail</strong> is missing, buy another from <strong>Vertida in the Myreque base for 20,000 coins</strong>.</p>
          <p>Mine/cut a ruby at Shilo if earlier Legends/jewellery used the last one. Buy <strong>one cosmic and five fire runes</strong> from Baba Yaga, use the standard spellbook for <strong>Lvl-3 Enchant</strong>, and take axe, knife and chisel. The base's crate supplies another silver sickle and the quest provides access to the Blisterwood tree; collect both during the quest.</p>
          <p>Bring a small stack of <strong>iron knives from Martin Thwait's Rogues' Den shop</strong> for the summoned bloodveld, instead of relying on random black knives from the defender grind. Refill food, prayer doses and useful combat potions using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> before Vanstrom, and repeat that bank check after an unsuccessful attempt.</p>
          <p><strong>Lost Drakan's medallion:</strong> before the final story sequence, Kael Forshaw can replace it in the old Myreque Hideout beneath the northern room of Old Man Ral's Meiyerditch house. <strong>After Sins of the Father, speak to Ivan Strom there instead</strong>. If the quest's current phase makes the free supplier unavailable, <strong>Perdu's Lost Property Shop sells a replacement for 30,000 coins</strong>; Perdu stands by Lumbridge Castle's southern wall. Bank a spare before Vanstrom if you want simple return travel after a death.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-slayer-51" number="32" title="Train Slayer from 50 to 51 for Troubled Tortugans">
        <p>Check your Slayer level and take ordinary tasks until <strong>unboosted 51</strong>. Troubled Tortugans requires that level to begin; its 8,000 Slayer XP reward comes after completion.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i25-tortugans" number="33" title="Complete Troubled Tortugans and unlock the Great Conch">
        <p>Return to the Sailing route introduced in 2.3. Check <strong>unboosted 51 Slayer, 48 Construction, 45 Sailing, 45 Hunter, 40 Woodcutting and 34 Crafting</strong>; the earlier chapters cover the other levels. You know the basic Sailing loop—board/manage your ship from a port, use its map and facilities, and bank or repair between trips—use the same routine for this quest. Begin the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Troubled_Tortugans" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Troubled Tortugans quest</a> and sail to its island story with combat supplies.</p>
        <p>For the <strong>Shellbane gryphon</strong>, assemble and equip the quest's <strong>Tortugan shield</strong> before the fight. Its melee hits are devastating without that shield even through Protect from Melee; with the shield and Protect from Melee, watch for its <strong>ranged and special attacks</strong>, keep food/restores, and use a comfortable melee setup/Piety with the gear you have. Wind Magic is a possible weakness but not a required switch. Claim <strong>10,000 Sailing and 8,000 Slayer XP</strong> and access to the <strong>Great Conch</strong>, the later Red Reef path.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover island tools and assemble the shield from quest materials">
          <p>Bring your <strong>axe, hammer and saw</strong> if banked. If missing, The Summer Shore has a <strong>bronze axe to the west</strong>, a <strong>hammer in the northeast smith's house</strong>, and a <strong>saw in Elder Raley's southeast house</strong>. A better owned axe speeds the cutting; no new axe grind is required.</p>
          <p>The island story supplies the seaweed, palm leaf and Tortugan-shield components. Finish that shield and equip it before the gryphon. Check food, a teleport and the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}> potion recipes and missing-stock recovery</a> immediately before the fight, and replace any doses used at Vanstrom.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">2.5 exit check</div>
        <h3>Piety unlocked; Morytania and the Great Conch open.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Temple Knight chain through <strong>The Slug Menace</strong>, Temple of the Eye and Zogre complete; <strong>full Legends' Quest</strong> complete after reaching 45 Herblore, with all four 30k rewards and the saved RFD lamp used on Herblore.</li>
          <li><strong>Ectophial, Salve (e), Proselyte, dragon defender and Barrows gloves</strong> kept; Warriors' Guild entry, unboosted 60+ Attack, Attack + Strength ≥130, unboosted 70 Defence/Prayer and <strong>Piety</strong> secured.</li>
          <li>Myreque chain through <strong>Sins of the Father</strong> complete; unboosted 54+ Agility, A Kingdom Divided and Book of the Dead, unboosted 60 Fletching, unboosted 50 Slayer and <strong>unboosted 60 Herblore before Sins</strong>; all six Sins choices allocated to Herblore.</li>
          <li><strong>Unboosted 51+ Slayer</strong>, Troubled Tortugans and Great Conch access. Keep Drakan's medallion and Blisterwood flail. Check your new Herblore, Slayer, combat and Sailing levels before continuing.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Stop Sailing here.</strong> Continue the 45→67 journey in 2.6, where it breaks up several skill-to-70 blocks.</p>
      </section>

